About Nebius:

Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.

Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.

Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;D.

The role

We’re &nbsp;looking for an outcome-driven&nbsp; Product Manager - Internal Billing Tools &nbsp;to own the reliability, scalability, and operational excellence of&nbsp; Nebius ’ internal billing systems. You will own the tools, processes, and automation that ensure billing is&nbsp; accurate , auditable, and fast for our internal teams and enterprise partners. &nbsp;

Your responsibilities will include: &nbsp;

Product Strategy &amp; Roadmap &nbsp;

• Own&nbsp;the roadmap for billing workflows, prioritizing initiatives based on risk, compliance, and scalability. &nbsp;

• Translate complex enterprise needs into a clear, prioritized product vision. &nbsp;

• Balance immediate operational fixes with long-term platform investments in billing integrity. &nbsp;

Discovery &amp; Research &nbsp;

• Run discovery with internal stakeholders (Finance, Support, Sales) and external partners (Resellers/SIs) to&nbsp;identify&nbsp;failure modes in the billing lifecycle. &nbsp;

• Validate automation ideas that replace manual work, such as quota management, billing account setup, and reconciliation. &nbsp;

• Synthesize regulatory requirements (SOX, GDPR/DSR) into functional product controls. &nbsp;

Execution &amp; Delivery &nbsp;

• Write concise PRDs and user stories for internal billing consoles, APIs, and reconciliation pipelines. &nbsp;

• Design and implement billing-specific&nbsp; RBAC/IAM models &nbsp;to ensure secure, least-privilege access for internal teams and partners. &nbsp;

• Leverage AI and automation tools to reduce manual operational hours and human error in billing corrections. &nbsp;

Cross-functional Leadership &amp; Measurement &nbsp;

• Align Engineering, Finance, Legal, and Partner Ops to deliver compliant, auditable billing flows. &nbsp;

• Define and own OKRs for billing health, including reconciliation gaps, partner onboarding time, and manual task reduction. &nbsp;

• Define operational SLAs and runbooks for billing incidents, ensuring high system uptime and data integrity. &nbsp;

We expect you to have: &nbsp;

Experience &nbsp;

• 5+ years of Product Management experience , specifically owning financial systems, billing, payments, or complex&nbsp;backoffice&nbsp;operations. &nbsp;

• Proven record of shipping automations that materially reduce manual operational hours. &nbsp;

• Experience in B2B/Enterprise domains, ideally involving reseller or partner-based billing models. &nbsp;

Technical Skills &nbsp;

• Deep domain knowledge of&nbsp; billing architectures : invoicing, ledger reconciliation, multi-tenant chargebacks, and pricing models. &nbsp;

• Technical fluency to partner with Engineering/SREs on RBAC/IAM, data pipelines, and API design. &nbsp;

• Ability to use SQL/analytics to diagnose operational issues and measure billing integrity. &nbsp;

Soft Skills &nbsp;

• Stakeholder management: &nbsp;Comfortable navigating the needs of Engineering, Finance, and Legal. &nbsp;

• Clarity in ambiguity: &nbsp;Able to translate high-level compliance or revenue goals into specific technical requirements. &nbsp;

• Customer empathy: &nbsp;A focus on the "internal customer," building tools that make our Ops and Support teams more efficient. &nbsp;

